{"id":"h104","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"claim","question":"Is the following claim true? The Rosetta Stone is held in the British Museum.","truth":"yes","model_answer":"yes","correct":true,"source":"author-written for this project; verified by the author","claims":[{"text":"The Rosetta Stone has been held by the British Museum in London since 1802.","confidence":0.98,"lean":1,"theta":1.5394,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The stone was surrendered to British forces under the Capitulation of Alexandria, ending the French occupation of Egypt.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The stone has been on public display at the British Museum continuously since then.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The Rosetta Stone is one of the British Museum's most visited objects.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The museum's collection records and public displays confirm its possession of the stone.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The 1802 transfer to Britain is well documented.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Egypt has requested its return and some argue it was taken unlawfully, but this concerns ownership, not location, so it does not falsify the claim.","confidence":0.9,"lean":0.1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The stone's Egyptian origin might be mistaken for its present location, but it is not in Egypt now.","confidence":0.92,"lean":1,"theta":1.4451,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The repatriation debate affects whether the stone should stay in the British Museum, not whether it is there.","confidence":0.92,"lean":1,"theta":1.4451,"phi":0.0}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.5,"relatio